1. Mono Example (Single Record)
Interview Question

What is Mono?

Practical Example

Traditional MVC

User user = repository.findById(id);
return user;


WebFlux

public Mono<User> getUser(Long id) {

    return userRepository
            .findById(id)
            .doOnNext(user ->
                    System.out.println("User Found : "
                    + user.getName()))
            .switchIfEmpty(
                    Mono.error(
                     new RuntimeException(
                            "User Not Found")));
}

Explanation
findById()
    |
returns Mono<User>

No DB call is executed yet

Only when subscribe() occurs
DB call executes


Interview One-Liner

Mono is a lazy asynchronous pipeline that produces zero or one element.

