3. WebClient Example
Interview Question

How do you call another microservice?

public Mono<User> getUser(Long id) {

    return webClient
            .get()
            .uri("/users/{id}", id)
            .retrieve()
            .bodyToMono(User.class);
}


Better Production Version

public Mono<User> getUser(Long id) {

    return webClient
            .get()
            .uri("/users/{id}", id)
            .retrieve()
            .bodyToMono(User.class)

            .timeout(Duration.ofSeconds(3))

            .retry(2)

            .onErrorResume(ex -> {

                User fallbackUser =
                        new User();

                fallbackUser.setName(
                        "DEFAULT USER");

                return Mono.just(fallbackUser);
            });
}


Interview One-Liner

WebClient supports non-blocking calls with timeout, retry and fallback.

4. Mono.zip Example
Most Important Senior Question

Requirement:

Need User
Need Department
Need Account

All APIs should execute together

Mono<User> userMono =
        userService.getUser(id);

Mono<Department> deptMono =
        departmentService.getDepartment(id);

Mono<Account> accountMono =
        accountService
                .getAccount(id);


Combine

return Mono.zip(
        userMono,
        deptMono,
        accountMono)
        .map(tuple -> {

            User user =
                    tuple.getT1();

            Department dept =
                    tuple.getT2();

            Account account =
                    tuple.getT3();

            return new UserResponse(
                    user,
                    dept,
                    account);
        });


Interview One-Liner

Mono.zip executes multiple non-blocking API calls concurrently and combines results.

