Important Interview Point First for Spring WebFLux Reactive Programming

-------------------------------------------------------------------------

✅ There is NO Reactive JPA.

Spring WebFlux + JPA/Hibernate is not fully reactive because JPA uses JDBC (blocking).
For a true reactive application use:
Spring WebFlux
Spring Data R2DBC
R2DBC H2 Driver

Your own WebFlux notes also indicate that reactive SQL access should use R2DBC repositories, not JPA repositories.

Interview One-Liner:

Spring WebFlux + JPA = NOT truly reactive
Spring WebFlux + R2DBC = Fully reactive


Also, Reactive repositories are not supported by JPA and require R2DBC-style repositories.

